{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791434114867,"sessionID":"ses_ee6357b88ffe0pZB3ogcBnOHmr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"campfire_add_finding","callID":"call_00_zsbkn10ldipilt16kez5vk6h","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"workspaceId":"ws_66892b28c1d640a8","summary":"Hypothesis: elevated IAD database latency is contributing to the /v1/exports timeouts. (not established)","detail":"Stated as a hypothesis, not fact. Supporting: IAD-only DB p95 elevation (140 -> 1090 -> 980 ms) coincides in time and region with IAD-only export 504s; the one sampled success (gw-101) spent 420 ms in DB. Against/limitation: the observed p95 is about 1 s, far below the 30000 ms gateway timeout, so a p95 of this size cannot by itself explain 30 s stalls, and the DB metric is all-routes_aggregate rather than export-specific. Would be confirmed by export-route-specific DB metrics or correlated traces showing near-30 s database time on failed requests (or connection-pool exhaustion). Would be refuted if failed exports show normal DB latency and stall elsewhere (or if failures occur before the application).","sourceArtifactId":"art_039c358aaf434d7c","confidence":0.35},"output":"{\n  \"createdBy\": {\n    \"actorId\": \"agt_f966eab3a01c47bb\",\n    \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n  },\n  \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_c5b74dd631a2449c\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:35:14.857Z\",\n  \"id\": \"find_59e9cd2eb5cd4c9a\",\n  \"workspaceId\": \"ws_66892b28c1d640a8\",\n  \"summary\": \"Hypothesis: elevated IAD database latency is contributing to the /v1/exports timeouts. (not established)\",\n  \"detail\": \"Stated as a hypothesis, not fact. Supporting: IAD-only DB p95 elevation (140 -> 1090 -> 980 ms) coincides in time and region with IAD-only export 504s; the one sampled success (gw-101) spent 420 ms in DB. Against/limitation: the observed p95 is about 1 s, far below the 30000 ms gateway timeout, so a p95 of this size cannot by itself explain 30 s stalls, and the DB metric is all-routes_aggregate rather than export-specific. Would be confirmed by export-route-specific DB metrics or correlated traces showing near-30 s database time on failed requests (or connection-pool exhaustion). Would be refuted if failed exports show normal DB latency and stall elsewhere (or if failures occur before the application).\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.35,\n  \"sourceArtifactId\": \"art_039c358aaf434d7c\",\n  \"currentness\": \"current\"\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791434114849,"end":1791434114864}},"id":"prt_119cb3e7c001QwKkm1Dh4w4XH7","sessionID":"ses_ee6357b88ffe0pZB3ogcBnOHmr","messageID":"msg_119cb3636001eU9QFSWuYyEj6e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791434116079,"sessionID":"ses_ee6357b88ffe0pZB3ogcBnOHmr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"campfire_add_finding","callID":"call_01_vbgfimfeo3xngw2nk2muzo63","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"workspaceId":"ws_66892b28c1d640a8","summary":"Hypothesis: the failing export requests may stall before reaching the application, or their application spans were simply not sampled. (inconclusive)","detail":"Stated as a hypothesis, not fact. The absence of application spans for gw-084 and gw-093 is consistent with a pre-application stall, but also fully consistent with the ~10% sampling rate. Would be resolved by capturing full (100%) traces for failed export request IDs and checking for app spans. Not currently supported either way.","sourceArtifactId":"art_7546bacd9f654b9d","confidence":0.2},"output":"{\n  \"createdBy\": {\n    \"actorId\": \"agt_f966eab3a01c47bb\",\n    \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n  },\n  \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_c5b74dd631a2449c\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:35:16.058Z\",\n  \"id\": \"find_4228073accd84466\",\n  \"workspaceId\": \"ws_66892b28c1d640a8\",\n  \"summary\": \"Hypothesis: the failing export requests may stall before reaching the application, or their application spans were simply not sampled. (inconclusive)\",\n  \"detail\": \"Stated as a hypothesis, not fact. The absence of application spans for gw-084 and gw-093 is consistent with a pre-application stall, but also fully consistent with the ~10% sampling rate. Would be resolved by capturing full (100%) traces for failed export request IDs and checking for app spans. Not currently supported either way.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.2,\n  \"sourceArtifactId\": \"art_7546bacd9f654b9d\",\n  \"currentness\": \"current\"\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791434116033,"end":1791434116072}},"id":"prt_119cb477c001v3XqsGckeJu7ke","sessionID":"ses_ee6357b88ffe0pZB3ogcBnOHmr","messageID":"msg_119cb3636001eU9QFSWuYyEj6e"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791434117578,"sessionID":"ses_ee6357b88ffe0pZB3ogcBnOHmr","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"campfire_add_finding","callID":"call_02_w258scg04xqdb80xej9rxneg","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"workspaceId":"ws_66892b28c1d640a8","summary":"Conclusion: the cause of the IAD /v1/exports timeouts is not established by the available evidence.","detail":"The evidence supports only that failures are IAD-scoped and time-coincident with a ~7x IAD database p95 elevation; there is no correlated gateway+application+database trace for any failed request, and the missing spans are uninformative at ~10% sampling. Unknowns: (1) whether failures occur inside the application or before it; (2) export-route-specific database latency, p99, and connection-pool state; (3) whether the 30000 ms stalls are caused by DB, connection saturation, or another upstream dependency. Resolving test: enable full sampling / capture correlated traces for failed /v1/exports request IDs and obtain export-specific database and pool metrics for IAD 09:40-10:00 UTC. No cause is asserted as fact.","confidence":0.6},"output":"{\n  \"createdBy\": {\n    \"actorId\": \"agt_f966eab3a01c47bb\",\n    \"actorType\": \"agent\"\n  },\n  \"agentSessionId\": \"ses_c5b74dd631a2449c\",\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-10-08T04:35:17.561Z\",\n  \"id\": \"find_5c5b5222d8d34862\",\n  \"workspaceId\": \"ws_66892b28c1d640a8\",\n  \"summary\": \"Conclusion: the cause of the IAD /v1/exports timeouts is not established by the available evidence.\",\n  \"detail\": \"The evidence supports only that failures are IAD-scoped and time-coincident with a ~7x IAD database p95 elevation; there is no correlated gateway+application+database trace for any failed request, and the missing spans are uninformative at ~10% sampling. Unknowns: (1) whether failures occur inside the application or before it; (2) export-route-specific database latency, p99, and connection-pool state; (3) whether the 30000 ms stalls are caused by DB, connection saturation, or another upstream dependency. Resolving test: enable full sampling / capture correlated traces for failed /v1/exports request IDs and obtain export-specific database and pool metrics for IAD 09:40-10:00 UTC. No cause is asserted as fact.\",\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"currentness\": \"current\"\n}","metadata":{"truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1791434117556,"end":1791434117574}},"id":"prt_119cb4bd0001omozhriTDW44Rs","sessionID":"ses_ee6357b88ffe0pZB3ogcBnOHmr","messageID":"msg_119cb3636001eU9QFSWuYyEj6e"}}
